UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION

vanilla-ultra-rag-mcp-server is an independent compatibility gateway built
directly on the UltraRAG project:

    UltraRAG
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG
    https://ultrarag.openbmb.cn/

UltraRAG's upstream README identifies it as a joint project of THUNLP at
Tsinghua University, NEUIR at Northeastern University, OpenBMB, and AI9stars,
together with the wider UltraRAG contributor community:

    https://nlp.csai.tsinghua.edu.cn/
    https://neuir.github.io/
    https://www.openbmb.cn/home
    https://github.com/AI9Stars
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG/graphs/contributors

This gateway relies on UltraRAG's MCP server architecture, tools, prompts,
pipeline design, and runtime. It currently pins and verifies:

    UltraRAG version 0.3.0.2
    commit 3a709a2aea3fbe46acca59c422621c94b6e86857
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG/tree/3a709a2aea3fbe46acca59c422621c94b6e86857

UltraRAG is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its license file
contains the notice "Copyright 2023 OpenBMB":

    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG/blob/3a709a2aea3fbe46acca59c422621c94b6e86857/LICENSE.txt
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The verified UltraRAG source snapshot downloaded by this gateway retains the
upstream LICENSE.txt and all upstream notices. No UltraRAG source file is
modified by this repository.

SUGGESTED SOFTWARE CITATION

The pinned UltraRAG revision does not include a dedicated UltraRAG BibTeX entry.
When citing the software, a suitable repository citation is:

    UltraRAG contributors. UltraRAG, version 0.3.0.2, commit
    3a709a2aea3fbe46acca59c422621c94b6e86857. OpenBMB/UltraRAG.
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG

For subject-specific academic citations, consult the Publications section in
UltraRAG's upstream README and cite the relevant original paper rather than
attributing those papers to this gateway.

